-- Fantasy Friends executable migration 20261115000010_definer_ownership_transfer
-- Generated by scripts/promote-migrations.mjs from supabase/design/migrations/011_definer_ownership_transfer.sql
-- Do not edit by hand: the guard re-derives this file and fails on drift.

-- PHASE 2B.5 DESIGN DRAFT. NOT A DEPLOYABLE MIGRATION. Do not place under
-- supabase/migrations or apply to a Supabase project.
--
-- Transfer ownership of all 56 SECURITY DEFINER functions to the dedicated
-- least-privilege definer role created by 009.
--
-- WHY THIS IS ONE FILE, AND WHY IT IS NOT A "BULK TRANSFER"
--   Every function gets the same target owner, but that is a conclusion reached
--   per function, not a shortcut. Measured in Phase 2B.5:
--     * 54 of the 56 read or write a public table DIRECTLY, so the definer's own
--       RLS visibility decides their behaviour;
--     * 2 (guard_standings, lock_roster_player) read no table directly, but they
--       delegate to require_leader / require_read_committed, which do;
--     * Postgres re-evaluates privileges PER FUNCTION against that function's
--       own owner (measured). A narrow wrapper does not constrain a broad helper,
--       so splitting owners by role would not shrink any privilege here - it
--       would only create 56 review surfaces.
--   The privilege actually being granted is: read/write public tables while
--   BYPASSING RLS, exactly as the current table-owner definer already does.
--   What changes is that the definer no longer OWNS the tables, so it can no
--   longer run DDL on them, and the privilege is declared instead of inherited.
--
-- ORDER: this must run AFTER 010. 010 asserts that ff_migration_owner is
-- NOLOGIN, has BYPASSRLS, owns no relation, and that exactly ten functions are
-- client-executable. Running 011 changes only the owner, so those assertions
-- still hold; but running it before 009/010 would leave the transfer unasserted.
--
-- This file performs NO grant changes. Grants and ownership are deliberately
-- separate steps so a failure is unambiguous (see the recovery runbook).

-- Guard: the target role must exist and must already be correct. If 009 did not
-- run, or the role was created without BYPASSRLS, the transfer would silently
-- break every read helper (they would return false for every real user), so
-- refuse instead of proceeding.
do $$
begin
  if not exists (select 1 from pg_roles where rolname = 'ff_migration_owner') then
    raise exception 'ff_migration_owner does not exist; apply 009 before 011' using errcode = '42501';
  end if;
  if exists (select 1 from pg_roles where rolname = 'ff_migration_owner' and (not rolbypassrls or rolcanlogin)) then
    raise exception 'ff_migration_owner must be NOLOGIN with BYPASSRLS before functions are transferred to it'
      using errcode = '42501';
  end if;
end $$;

